# Day 11

**26km / 6 hours**

Started early today to make the most of the time in Kerikeri for all the chores and preparation required for the next day. The downside was getting up while it was cold and dark but once I got going the sun had risen and moving around warmed me up.

![A nice photo I took of a tree during the sunrise](./sunrise-tree.jpg)

We walked a bit on the road and over farms, which was quite pleasant although not really that exciting; the nicest parts were when the farm trail came across a special part such as the water pool as shown.

![A nice little water pool along the farm](./water-pool.jpg)

After that was a long walk into Kerikeri that seemed to go on for ages, especially considering how early we saw houses on the outer edge. The river trail was exceptional in normal situations but when tired and carrying a large pack it was a bit painful to do.

![A proper waterfall at Rainbow Falls in Kerikeri](./waterfall.jpg)